---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import { NAV_GROUPS } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="How Better Ibaan is built to be usable with keyboard, reduced motion, and map fallbacks."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'About' }, { label: 'Accessibility' }]}
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Usable without the extra effects."
    intro="This page describes the accessibility choices in Better Ibaan. It is a working note, not a formal conformance claim."
    note="If something on this site blocks you, the underlying municipal source is always linked and can be used directly."
  >
    <Toc
      items={[
        { id: 'navigation', label: 'Navigation' },
        { id: 'map', label: 'Map fallback' },
        { id: 'motion', label: 'Motion and contrast' },
        { id: 'limits', label: 'Limits' },
      ]}
    />
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="section-tight" id="navigation">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="prose-wide">
        <h2>Keyboard and landmarks</h2>
        <p>
          The header, main content, navigation, and footer are separate landmarks. A skip link is
          available before the header. Menus, search, source notes, and service lists use native
          buttons and disclosure elements, so they work with a keyboard without custom key handlers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every page is reachable from the header menu and the footer directory. The
          <a href="/sitemap">sitemap</a> lists the same routes in one place.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" id="map">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="prose-wide">
        <h2>Map fallback</h2>
        <p>
          The interactive barangay map needs WebGL and tile access. If either is unavailable, the
          page keeps a flat SVG outline of the same 26 barangays with a text index. The 2D view is
          also available from the map toolbar in the WebGL view.
        </p>
        <p>
          Map controls have text labels and state changes are announced through pressed states. The
          map is an orientation aid; all barangay names are also available as a table on the
          <a href="/barangays">barangays page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" id="motion">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="prose-wide">
        <h2>Motion and contrast</h2>
        <p>
          When reduced motion is requested, entrance animations and smooth scrolling are disabled.
          The light and dark themes are explicit choices and both use high-contrast text on quiet
          backgrounds. Type is self-hosted so the page does not depend on a third-party font service.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" id="limits">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Limits of this note</strong>
        <p>
          No automated accessibility audit is claimed here. External municipal pages and social
          links follow their own accessibility practices and are outside this site.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-card-grid">
        {NAV_GROUPS.map((group) => (
          <a class="nav-card" href={group.href}>
            <strong>{group.label}</strong>
            <span>{group.blurb}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
